# Digital Safe Lock using Verilog HDL

## Overview

This project implements a Digital Safe Lock using Verilog HDL. The safe unlocks only when the correct 4-bit password is entered. If the password is incorrect, the safe remains locked.

## Features

- 4-bit password authentication
- Lock and Unlock indication
- Reset functionality
- Simple FSM-based design
- Easy FPGA implementation

## Inputs

| Signal | Width | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| clk | 1 | Clock Signal |
| reset | 1 | Active High Reset |
| password | 4 | User Password |

## Outputs

| Signal | Width | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| unlock | 1 | Safe Unlock Indicator |

## Default Password

```
1010 (Decimal 10)
```

## Truth Table

| Reset | Password | Unlock |
|-------|----------|--------|
|1|XXXX|0|
|0|1010|1|
|0|Others|0|

## Applications

- Electronic Safe
- Digital Locker
- Security Systems
- Bank Lockers
- Smart Homes

